<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artemisia I of Caria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 480 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artemisia I was the queen of Halicarnassus in Caria in the early 5th century BCE, ruling as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> after the death of her husband. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, himself from Halicarnassus, describes how she commanded five ships in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a>' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a> and fought at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-salamis">Battle of Salamis</a> in 480 BCE, having advised the king against giving battle. She was the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lygdamis-i">Lygdamis I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artemisia-i-of-caria.jpg" alt="Artemisia I of Caria" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaulbach, Wilhelm von, 19th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artemisia_at_the_Battle_of_Salamis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
